    "title": "rpc: fix dumptxoutset rollback crash after loadtxoutset on pruned node",
    "user": {
      "login": "FlashWayne",
      "id": 332458478,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOE9Dp7g",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/332458478?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/FlashWayne",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/FlashWayne/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "On a pruned node, `dumptxoutset` with `rollback` checks that the blocks it needs haven't been pruned by calling `GetFirstBlock(*current_tip, BLOCK_HAVE_MASK)` (blockchain.cpp:3194). `GetFirstBlock` asserts that the block it starts from has both block and undo data (blockstorage.cpp:638).\r\n\r\nRight after `loadtxoutset`, the active tip is the snapshot base block, and that has neither until it's downloaded. So on a `-prune` node:\r\n\r\n```\r\nloadtxoutset <snapshot>\r\ndumptxoutset <path> rollback=<height>\r\n```\r\n\r\naborts bitcoind:\r\n\r\n```\r\nAssertion failed: ((last_block->nStatus & status_mask) == status_mask), function GetFirstBlock, file blockstorage.cpp, line 638.\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe `GetPruneHeight` helper already guards against a tip without data (blockchain.cpp:934), this call site doesn't.\r\n\r\nThis returns the existing \"Could not roll back to requested height since necessary block data is already pruned.\" error when the tip itself has no data, before calling `GetFirstBlock`.\r\n\r\nThe test goes in `feature_assumeutxo.py`, right after the snapshot is loaded on the pruned node (node 1): `dumptxoutset` with a rollback to the start height must return that error. On master the RPC times out because the node aborted. With the fix `feature_assumeutxo.py` and `rpc_dumptxoutset.py` pass.\r\n\r\n",
